# Own-wording spells of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2014 rules), part A. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Abduct": ["1 mile, 1 hour. Teleport a creature known to you next to you. An unwilling target makes a Charisma save.",
 "1 mile, 1 hour. Choose a creature known to you within range. An unwilling target makes a Charisma save to resist. On a failure it appears at a spot you choose within 30 ft of you, and you choose whether it sits, stands, lies prone or is bound by nearby restraints. When the spell ends you decide whether it stays or returns to where it was taken from."],
"Aberrate": ["Self, 1 minute. Critical hits do no extra damage to you, and after taking damage you can use your Reaction to gain Resistance to that type.",
 "Self, 1 minute. Your body keeps reshaping itself into new horrors. You take no extra damage from critical hits. Right after you take damage, you can use your Reaction to gain Resistance to that damage type until the spell ends or until you use this Reaction again for a different type. The Resistance does not cover the triggering damage."],
"Accelerate/Decelerate": ["Reaction, 60 ft. Raise or lower the damage a target takes from an attack by 1d6 + your spellcasting modifier.",
 "Reaction, 60 ft. You speed or slow an attack just before it lands. Accelerate: the target takes extra damage equal to 1d6 + your spellcasting ability modifier. Decelerate: the target takes that much less damage, to a minimum of 0." + HL + "The change grows by 1d6 for each slot level above 1."],
"Accursed Act": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A cursed creature takes 1d8 + your modifier psychic damage once per turn when it attacks or casts a spell.",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You light a candle and speak dark curses at a creature you see. It makes a Wisdom save or is cursed. While cursed, it takes psychic damage equal to 1d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier once per turn when it attacks or casts a spell. If it does neither on its turn, it repeats the save at the end of that turn and ends the curse on a success. Remove Curse ends it." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 1."],
"Action": ["30 ft, 1 round. A willing creature gains an extra action next turn: one weapon attack, Dash, Disengage, Hide or Use an Object.",
 "30 ft, 1 round. Choose a willing creature you see. On its next turn it gains one extra action, usable only for the Attack action (one weapon attack), Dash, Disengage, Hide or Use an Object."],
"Aerial Alacrity": ["60 ft, 10 minutes. A flying target can Dash as a Bonus Action, hover, has Advantage on Acrobatics and provokes no opportunity attacks by flying away.",
 "60 ft, 10 minutes. Choose a willing creature with a flying Speed (natural, temporary or magical). For the duration it can Dash as a Bonus Action, it can hover, it has Advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks, and it provokes no opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach."],
"After Image": ["Self, 10 minutes. An illusory double may take hits for you: when hit, roll a die and on odd the double takes it.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. You create an illusory duplicate that mirrors your moves. When an attack hits you, roll any die. On an odd result, the attack hits the duplicate instead and it vanishes. It returns after you move 10 feet or more or take the Dodge action. On an even result the attack hits you as normal."],
"Antiballistics Field": ["40 ft, Concentration, 10 minutes. A 40 ft radius field makes firearms inside jam and weakens shots fired into it.",
 "40 ft, Concentration, 10 minutes. An invisible 40-foot-radius field of magic spreads from you. Inside it, firearm attacks fail and the firearm jams at once. A jammed firearm cannot attack until a creature uses an action to clear it. Firearms outside the field that fire into it have Disadvantage on attack rolls and deal half damage on a hit."],
"Arc Blade": ["Cantrip, 5 ft. Melee weapon attack with lightning damage, and an arc jumps to a creature within 5 ft of the target for 1d6.",
 "5 ft. As part of the casting action, make a melee weapon attack against a creature within range, or the spell fails. On a hit, the attack deals lightning damage instead of its usual type, and an arc of lightning jumps to a creature you choose within 5 feet of the target for 1d6 lightning damage.\n\nAt level 5, the melee attack deals an extra 1d8 lightning damage and the arc deals an extra 1d6. Both rise again at level 11 (2d8 and 3d6) and level 17 (3d8 and 4d6)."],
"Arcane Anomaly": ["30 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Whenever a spell is cast within range, roll a d6: on a 1 it fails and the slot is spent.",
 "30 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You crack the magical energy of the multiverse. For the duration, whenever a spell is cast within range, roll a d6. On a 1 the casting fails. The caster still spends the spell slot, but costly material components are not consumed."],
"Arcane Capacitor": ["Touch. Melee spell attack for 5d10 force damage, then you regain an expended 1st-level slot.",
 "Touch. You channel arcane power into your fingertips and recycle the surplus into a new slot. Make a melee spell attack against a creature you can reach. On a hit it takes 5d10 force damage. Hit or miss, you regain one expended 1st-level spell slot." + HL + "With a 7th-level slot you regain a 2nd-level slot instead. With a 9th-level slot you regain a 3rd-level slot instead."],
"Benign Dismemberment": ["Touch, 1 hour, 1 minute cast. A willing target's body parts can be severed harmlessly and reattached.",
 "Touch, 1 hour, casting time 1 minute. For the duration, a willing target's body parts (fingers, legs, tail, even its head) can be cut off without harm, provided the cut is swift and clean. The head stays alive and conscious, and parts connected to it stay alive. Severed parts become inanimate but do not decay for the duration. Holding a severed part to its stump instantly reattaches it. When the spell ends, parts still severed stay severed for good. The target dies if vital organs are not reattached to its head."],
"Blood Print": ["Touch. Wet blood on a surface forms a unique print and reveals the kind of creature it came from.",
 "Touch. At your touch, wet blood on a surface shifts into a pattern of crimson blotches. The print is unique to the creature the blood belongs to, and from its shape you learn the creature's kind (human, gnoll, deer, fire giant and so on). You can preserve a print by pressing paper against it. Cast twice, the spell lets you match blood samples from the same creature by comparing prints."],
"Boomering": ["30 ft. Ranged spell attack for 3d6 radiant, one reroll on a miss. Higher slots ricochet to more targets.",
 "30 ft. A ring of sparks leaves your hand and ricochets back to you. Make a ranged spell attack against a creature in range. On a hit it takes 3d6 radiant damage. If you miss, you can repeat the attack against the same target once." + HL + "The damage rises by 3d6 for each slot level above 1. With a 3rd-level slot or higher, after hitting the first target the ring ricochets to a second target you see within 30 feet of the first and deals damage on a hit. With a 5th-level slot or higher it can ricochet to a third target within 30 feet of the second. You can repeat the attack roll against only one target in total."],
"Burning Blade": ["Cantrip, 5 ft, 1 round. Melee weapon attack with fire damage and embers that burn creatures entering the space.",
 "5 ft, 1 round. As part of the casting action, make a melee weapon attack against a creature within range, or the spell fails. On a hit, the attack deals fire damage instead of its usual type, and embers whirl in the target's space. Until the start of your next turn, when a creature enters the space for the first time or ends its turn there, you can use your Reaction to deal 1d6 fire damage to it, ending the spell.\n\nAt level 5, the attack deals an extra 1d6 fire damage and the embers deal an extra 1d6. Both rise again at level 11 (2d6 and 3d6) and level 17 (3d6 and 4d6)."],
"Burnt Offering": ["Self, 24 hours, 10 minute cast. Add Wisdom instead of Dexterity to AC while armored. Higher slots add a saving throw reroll.",
 "Self, 24 hours, casting time 10 minutes. Build a pyre and burn an animal's corpse to court the gods' favor. For the duration, while you wear armor you add your Wisdom modifier to your AC instead of your Dexterity modifier." + HL + "With a 3rd-level slot or higher you can also reroll one saving throw during the duration. You choose after rolling, before the result is determined, and you must use the new roll."],
"Candy Blast": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 1d8 bludgeoning, and the target's 5 ft square becomes difficult terrain.",
 "60 ft. You conjure a handful of hard candy and hurl it at a target you see. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 bludgeoning damage, and the 5-foot square it stands in becomes difficult terrain until a creature uses an action to gather the candy. The candy is edible but has no nutrition.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d8 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Card Trick": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. Choose a ranged spell attack or a Dexterity save: 1d6 force damage.",
 "60 ft. You fling a playing or tarot card charged with energy. Choose whether you make a ranged spell attack or the target makes a Dexterity save. On a hit or failed save the target takes 1d6 force damage.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d6 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Caustic Blade": ["Cantrip, 5 ft. Melee weapon attack with acid damage, and a near miss still splashes 1d8 acid.",
 "5 ft. As part of the casting action, make a melee weapon attack against a creature within range, or the spell fails. On a hit, the attack deals acid damage instead of its usual type. If you miss by 3 or less, acid splashes the target for 1d8 acid damage instead.\n\nAt level 5, the attack deals an extra 1d8 acid damage on a hit and the miss damage becomes 2d8. Both rise again at level 11 (2d8 and 3d8) and level 17 (3d8 and 4d8)."],
"Cerebral Ray": ["60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 2d10 psychic and Disadvantage on ability checks until your next turn.",
 "60 ft. A violet beam streaks to a creature in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 2d10 psychic damage and has Disadvantage on ability checks until the start of your next turn." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d10 for each slot level above 1."],
"Cheat": ["Bonus Action, self, 1 round. Reroll ability checks made for nonmagical games of chance.",
 "Self, 1 round. You twist your fingers and fate follows. For the duration you can reroll any ability check you make to play nonmagical games of chance. It can sway a poker game but not a Deck of Many Things."],
"Chromatic Bullet": ["Bonus Action, self, Concentration, 1 minute. Your next firearm hit adds 2d4 elemental damage and can change the firearm's damage type.",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. The next time you hit with a ranged weapon attack using a firearm during the duration, the bullet sparks with elemental energy and deals an extra 2d4 damage. You choose acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison or thunder for the extra damage, and you can change the firearm's own damage to one of these types. The two types need not match." + HL + "The extra damage rises by 2d4 for each slot level above 1."],
"Clue": ["Touch, 10 minutes. Footprints and fingerprints from up to 10 days back glow in a 45 ft radius, each creature in its own color.",
 "Touch, 10 minutes. All footprints and fingerprints within 45 feet of a point you touch glow faintly for the duration. At casting you choose a time span of up to the last 10 days, and only marks left in that span glow. Each creature that left marks gets its own color, with no identification. Creatures that move or touch things in the area also leave colorful marks, which can reveal invisible creatures."],
"Concealed Shot": ["Cantrip, self. A ranged weapon attack whose projectile is invisible and silent, hiding a firearm's smoke and flash.",
 "Self. As part of the casting action, make an attack with a ranged weapon, or the spell fails. The projectile is invisible in flight and the weapon is silent. For a firearm, the spell hides the smoke and light it gives off, so no one can see or hear where the shot came from. It conceals only the first shot you make."],
"Conjure Cannonball": ["600 ft. Spell attack for 4d10 bludgeoning, and creatures within 5 ft make a Dexterity save for half.",
 "600 ft. You summon a cannonball in mid-flight at full speed, and it explodes on impact. Make a spell attack against a target you see in range. On a hit it takes 4d10 bludgeoning damage, and each creature within 5 feet of the target makes a Dexterity save, taking half as much damage on a failure. " + HL + "The damage rises by 1d10 for each slot level above 3."],
"Conjure Cover": ["10 ft, Concentration, 1 hour, Bonus Action. A low cobblestone wall of three 5 ft segments gives cover.",
 "10 ft, Concentration, 1 hour. You conjure a low cobblestone wall on the ground at a point you see. It is 18 inches thick and made of three 5-foot-long, 3-foot-high segments, each touching at least one other. A Medium creature hunkering behind it has cover from ranged attacks, as does a Small creature, and a prone creature has total cover. The wall can be leapt over at no extra movement cost. Each segment has AC 10 and 60 hit points and crumbles at 0. The wall vanishes when all segments are gone or the spell ends."],
"Consecrated Armor": ["Self, 8 hours. Base AC 12 + Dex, or 15 + Dex against Fiends and Undead.",
 "Self, 8 hours. You trace a holy symbol on your chest and an invisible barrier shields you. Your base AC becomes 12 + your Dexterity modifier, or 15 + your Dexterity modifier against attacks from a Fiend or Undead. You can use it if your worn armor would give a lower AC. A shield works as normal."],
"Corruption Curse": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Curse a creature with Disadvantage on Dexterity, Constitution or Wisdom rolls of your pick.",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You send a ribbon of dark magic into a creature you see. It is cursed for the duration and suffers one effect of your choice:\n- Dull Reflexes. Disadvantage on Dexterity checks and saves.\n- Feeble Fortitude. Disadvantage on Constitution saves, and it cannot regain hit points.\n- Weak Will. Disadvantage on Wisdom saves and spell attack rolls.\nRemove Curse cast with a 6th-level slot or higher ends it."],
"Cryptogram": ["Cantrip, unlimited range. Send a scroll with an 8 character message to a known creature on your plane, once per day per target.",
 "Unlimited range. You send a small scroll with a short message to a creature known to you on the same plane. It hovers before the recipient, drops into a pocket or appears on something nearby. The message holds up to 8 characters, spaces included. You can send only one scroll to a given target per day."],
"Curse Ward": ["Touch, 1 hour. Necrotic Resistance, and the target cannot be cursed, possessed, hexed or have its hit point maximum reduced.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You touch a willing creature and raise a smoky barrier around it. For the duration it has Resistance to necrotic damage and cannot be cursed, possessed or targeted by a hex, and its hit point maximum cannot be reduced. If it is already under one of these effects, the effect is suspended until the spell ends."],
"Curse of Binding": ["60 ft, permanent. Bind a creature or object to a place. A creature past 20 ft is dragged back.",
 "60 ft, until dispelled. You bind a creature or object you see to a location you see, so it can never leave. A creature makes a Charisma save (a willing one can fail). Cursed, it can move and act freely within 20 feet of the bound point. If it starts its turn outside that area it makes a Strength save against your spell save DC or is dragged 60 feet toward the point. If it tries extraplanar travel it makes another Charisma save, and on a failure the attempt fails and resources are wasted. On a success the curse is suppressed until it returns to the plane where it was bound. Remove Curse cast with a 7th-level slot or higher ends it."],
"Curse of Blades": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A creature cannot drop its weapon and makes an extra attack against itself when it attacks.",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Bands of black energy tie a creature to its weapon. Choose a creature you see holding a weapon. It makes a Wisdom save or is cursed. A cursed creature cannot willingly drop or stow the weapon. Whenever it takes the Attack action, it makes one extra attack with that weapon against itself, against its own AC, dealing damage on a hit. Remove Curse ends it."],
"Curse of Chains": ["120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Two creatures within 30 ft of each other cannot willingly move farther apart.",
 "120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A black brand like iron shackles darkens the ankles of creatures you see. Choose two creatures within range and within 30 feet of each other. Each makes a Constitution save (a willing one can fail). On a failure it is cursed. If only one is cursed, on a later turn you can use an action or Bonus Action to choose another creature within 30 feet of it to save. While two creatures are cursed, they cannot willingly move farther from each other. Remove Curse ends it."],
"Dazzling Ray": ["60 ft, 1 round. Up to three ranged spell attacks blind the targets until the spell ends.",
 "60 ft, 1 round. Three rays of brilliant color shoot at up to three creatures you see. Make a ranged spell attack for each ray. A hit blinds the target until the spell ends." + HL + "You create one extra ray for each slot level above 2, to a maximum of 6 rays."],
"Dead Fog": ["120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A 15 ft fog of Dead Mists deals 3d8 necrotic and can hold creatures in. Pay hit points to cast it higher.",
 "120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A 15-foot-radius sphere of fog filled with the necromantic Dead Mists appears at a point you see. It spreads around corners and its area is heavily obscured. It lasts for the duration or until strong wind disperses it.\n\nWhen you cast it you can lose 10, 15 or 20 hit points to empower it. Treat the slot as 1, 2 or 3 levels higher respectively, up to 9th.\n\nWhen a creature enters the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it makes a Constitution save, taking 3d8 necrotic damage on a failure. When a creature tries to leave, you can have the fog grasp it. It makes a Strength save and cannot move on a failure." + HL + "The damage rises by 3d8 for each slot level above 3."],
"Dead Mist Lash": ["60 ft. Ranged spell attack for 3d8 necrotic. Pay 5, 10 or 15 hit points to cast it higher.",
 "60 ft. You conjure a glowing white tendril of the Dead Mists that lashes at a foe you see. When you cast it you can lose 5, 10 or 15 hit points. Treat the slot as one level higher for every 5 hit points lost, up to 9th. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 3d8 necrotic damage." + HL + "The damage rises by 3d8 for each slot level above 1."],
"Defenestration": ["30 ft. Strength save or thrown 20 ft through a window for 4d6 slashing; on a success, pushed 5 ft.",
 "30 ft. A wave of force hurls a creature you see through a window. It makes a Strength save. On a failure it is thrown up to 20 feet through a window you choose. If no window is within 20 feet, it is thrown through a window of force that forms 10 feet behind it and vanishes after it shatters. It takes 4d6 slashing damage as it passes through. On a success it is pushed back 5 feet and takes no damage." + HL + "The creature is pushed an extra 5 feet for each slot level above 2."],
}
